# 4. ⚙️ Feasibility of Execution

## Can This Be Built Within a Hackathon?

The core MVP components are technically feasible within a hackathon. However, advanced clinical validation and large-scale healthcare deployment should be considered future phases.

| Component | Feasibility |
|---|---:|
| 📱 **Mobile Application** | 🟢 Very High |
| 🧠 **Cognitive Games** | 🟢 Very High |
| ⏰ **Reminder System** | 🟢 Very High |
| 👨‍👩‍👧 **Caregiver Dashboard** | 🟢 High |
| 🤖 **Adaptive Difficulty** | 🟢 High |
| 📴 **Offline Database** | 🟢 High |
| 🎙️ **Voice Interface** | 🟢 High |
| 🌐 **Multilingual Content** | 🟢 High |
| 📊 **AI-Based Cognitive Performance Analysis** | 🟡 Medium |
| 🩺 **Clinically Validated Dementia Detection** | 🔴 Low |

### 💡 Feasibility Insight

The hackathon MVP should focus on **cognitive engagement, personalization, caregiver support, multilingual accessibility, and offline functionality** rather than attempting to build a clinically validated dementia-diagnosis system.
